  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fix TpapTransport swallowing caller cancellation: SendAsync and the keepalive path caught TaskCanceledException as a generically \"retryable\" condition and unconditionally reset the session and retried the request (including a full handshake), even when the exception was caused by the caller's own external CancellationToken rather than the internal per-request timeout. This meant an external cancellation request could be silently absorbed by a retry attempt instead of propagating immediately, causing callers with a short requested cancellation timeout to still experience the full duration of a new handshake+request cycle. Both paths now only reset/retry when the external token was not the cause of the cancellation; a genuine external cancellation now propagates immediately as OperationCanceledException.",
  "repository": {
